[0m$ [0mgh issue comment 66 --body "## App verified on port 3000 — CDN works, 3D gameplay live

Play locally: http://127.0.0.1:3000/ (tmux session app-server, node server, serves ./index.html as 200, 107270 bytes).

Root cause (issue investigation): there is no Three.js CDN download failure in this worker. All three exact dependency URLs return HTTP 200 with correct bytes/hashes from the SSH worker session (unpkg three.min.js 669884 bytes sha256 170c6789...49fa; jsdelivr+unpkg three.module.js 1272972 bytes sha256 76dea815...a495). The only failing layer ever observed is WebGL context creation in GPU-less headless Chrome, which the game correctly converts to its 2D fallback. Full evidence: PROGRESS_CDN_INVESTIGATION.md.

End-to-end proof just now (headless Chrome for Testing 152 + SwiftShader, served over http):
- Title/vehicle-select renders (NEON SCRAPYARD, 3 rides, START ENGINE).
- Autostart gameplay renders live 3D: arena, towers, vehicles, HUD (HULL/TURBO 100, weapons, KILLS 0/5, ENEMIES 5, MINIMAP).
- Console: only benign three.min.js deprecation INFO + SwiftShader perf notes. Zero net errors, zero uncaught.
- Entrypoint ./index.html is byte-identical to committed build e889141 (sha256 b15e5557...433a5); inline JS node --check PASS.

Fixes applied this pass:
- Created missing ./index.html (restored verified e889141 build; branch had none).
- app-server: python3 -m http.server left CLOSED sockets in this sandbox, so tmux app-server now runs a minimal node static server on port 3000 (verified 200 on / and /index.html).
- Same node server initially 404'd query-string URLs (?autostart=1); fixed to strip query before file lookup, re-verified byte-identical 200.

Screenshots: screenshots/final-title.png, screenshots/final-gameplay.png (committed on the project branch by the workflow).
Known limitations: loopback python http.server does not bind-usably here (node used instead); public tunnel URL is ephemeral; deprecation warn from three r160 min.js is benign." 2>&1 | tail -n 3
